                        "entry_id": "7af371f9-b910-3fc5-9ef5-f759006cbd67",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Any of a group of economists in 18th-century France who believed that the government should not seek to influence the operation of natural economic laws."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "historical"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "77dc93e0-dae6-488b-b3c1-0421278d5800",
                                "sense_id": "2185ce9e-3f1e-37bc-9bb2-aa1fd60e0f66",
                                "text": "The Physiocrats espoused a professional service ethic and, in the interests of societal welfare, sought to establish laws of political economy and social relations."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d9d541aa-700b-44b5-916d-5e22127d15e6",
                                "sense_id": "2185ce9e-3f1e-37bc-9bb2-aa1fd60e0f66",
                                "text": "Smith spent some time in Paris and got to know the physiocrats personally, notably François Quesnay and Anne-Robert-Jacques Turgot."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
